Z||000000||RZURCTN||10-07-1999||06:59 PM||||I have come to the conclusion that it is time to swap the engine in my 84SE.  It wasn't too well taken care of and seems rather abused, kinda like someone ran it out of oil on a regular basis.  The build up of sludge under the valve cover is 1/4" thick in places!!!  It will require a complete rebuild, and since I am doing this one under a budget(have a bun in the oven that is due in Nov.) I don't have all the money I would like to do a complete rebuid.  I can pick up another motor for $250.  Put that in the car and I'll be back on the road with a grin on my face!  Until then.....(sniff).....I get to look at it sitting there.  Does anyone make a Fiero Teddybear?  Something a guy can cling to, kind of like a passifier?  I could use one of those!||||reg||9
